0. Overview
-----------

    Braving is an independently branded browser based on exact Brave
    and Chromium releases, featuring a maintainable patch-based architecture.

    Braving does not simply rebrand an APK. It builds directly from clean
    upstream source code with reproducible, patch-driven modifications.


1. Architecture Overview
------------------------

    User selects BRAVE_VERSION
              |
    matching brave-core release
              |
    exact Chromium revision
              |
    Braving patches
              |
    Braving source
              |
    reproducible Braving build
              |
    Braving APK / AAB


2. Repository Structure
-----------------------

    braving/
    |-- android/                 Override sources & configs
    |-- patches/                 Directory containing source code patches
    |   |-- branding/            App identity, strings, package name, icons
    |   |-- build/               GN arguments, toolchain settings, manifest
    |   |-- features/            Feature disabling (Wallet, Ads, Rewards, VPN)
    |   |-- origin/              Minimal / origin policy configurations
    |   `-- telemetry/           Disable P3A analytics and metrics reporting
    |-- scripts/                 Build and validation scripts
    |   |-- build-android.sh     Phase 2: Compiles the Braving APK
    |   |-- generate-icons.sh    Generates launcher icons
    |   |-- prepare-source.sh    Phase 1: Validates revisions & applies patches
    |   |-- verify-all.sh        Runs all verifications
    |   |-- verify-branding.sh   Lints for unintentional Brave trademark remnants
    |   `-- verify-patches.sh    Verifies patch integrity
    |-- metadata/                Release manifests and exact upstream commits
    |-- docs/                    Project documentation and guidelines
    |-- tests/                   Automated build & branding tests
    |-- .gitlab-ci.yml           Two-phase GitLab CI pipeline
    `-- LICENSE                  MPL-2.0


3. Building Braving
-------------------

3.1. Prerequisites

    Building Braving requires a Linux environment (x86_64 or aarch64).
    You will need the following tools installed:

      - Node.js >= 24.16.0
      - pnpm >= 11.11.0
      - Python 3.10+
      - JDK 17+
      - Android SDK & NDK (for mobile builds)


3.2. Prepare Source

    To validate revisions, checkout the source code, and apply Braving
    branding patches, run the preparation script with the desired
    Brave version:

        ./scripts/prepare-source.sh 1.94.120


3.3. Build Braving APK

    Once the source is prepared, you can start the compilation
    process. This step handles GN configuration and Ninja compilation:

        ./scripts/build-android.sh --arch=arm64 --release


4. Special Thanks
-----------------

    Braving would not be possible without the incredible work and
    resources provided by others. Special thanks to:

      - Brave Software (https://brave.com/) for their excellent
        open-source browser code and privacy-preserving Shields.
        Their commitment to open source makes this project possible.

      - GitLab (https://gitlab.com/) for providing generous and robust
        Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)
        infrastructure that powers our automated reproducible builds.


